  "story": "Imagine a magical mirror that, when you look into it, it shows you not just your reflection, but also a smaller version of itself looking back at you. This smaller mirror does the same, and so on, until you reach a tiny mirror that just shows a small part of itself. Each mirror is a copy of the original, but smaller. The Fibonacci sequence is like a series of these mirrors, each one showing a part of the whole sequence.",
